lib/OCP/Cmd/Hetzner/List.pm line 55 calls $server->server_type->{name}. WWW::Hetzner::Cloud::Server->server_type returns the type name as a plain string (the raw hash is server_type_data), so the command dies under strict refs ("Can't use string (\"cx22\") as a HASH ref") as soon as one server is listed. Reproduced offline against a fake IO while writing the consumer skill perl-www-hetzner (p5-www-hetzner k35).

Done when: the column reads $server->server_type, and a test lists a server through a fake IO (pattern in skill perl-www-hetzner, "Tests without network").

